    "text": "AZFamily\nwebsite\nPhoenix\nReport: Pilot made mayday calls, couldn’t see airport before deadly crash of Phoenix-bound flight\nBy Alexis Cortez,\n11 hours agoPHOENIX (AZFamily) — A preliminary report shows what led up to a plane crash that left six people dead on a flight to Phoenix last month. On June 8 around 12:30 p.m., a twin-engine Cessna 414 crashed roughly three miles off the coast of Point Loma, a San Diego neighborhood, on its way back to Phoenix. Jeremy Bingham and his three sons, Bailey, Gavin and Ayden, were killed. The pilot and his pregnant wife also died in the crash.\n21",
